# m1_pool_new
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: seal::util::MemoryPoolHeadMT::get()
# cost_class: paid
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# basis      published decomposition = one row, MemoryPoolHeadMT::get() (SEAL pool), 99.3% of 384.29 GiB.
#            Pool census (impl/p_poolcensus.md, job 45956540; free list = retained part):
#              layer 0 START   191 size classes   pool took 164.8 GiB    free   6.5 GiB =  3.9%
#              layer 0 END     236 size classes   pool took 399.5 GiB    free 176.9 GiB = 44.3%
#            free list by class:
#              36,700,160 B x 2,411   of which  805 free   27.51 GiB     2 polys x 35 limbs
#              23,068,672 B x 1,568   of which  781 free   16.78 GiB
#              22,020,096 B x 1,568   of which  780 free   16.00 GiB     2 polys x 21 limbs, a level-20 CT
#              ... 233 further classes
#            whole released ciphertexts kept by the pool (not fragmentation). items x size = taken from
#            the allocator, not resident (exceeds RSS); the free fraction is unaffected.
# mechanism  SEAL MemoryManager profile MMProfGlobal: one global pool, never returns memory. This SEAL
#            (4.1-bs) has MMProfGlobal, MMProfNew, MMProfFixed, MMProfThreadLocal; no threshold profile
#            (the earlier campaign's "MMProfThreshold" was its own patch).
# lever      MMProfNew (new/delete per allocation). One line, stock SEAL.
# expected   up to 176.9 GiB off 384.29 GiB (~46%); less if the peak is not at the layer boundary or glibc
#            arenas retain.
# cost       declared paid (n=1): new/delete per ciphertext-sized object instead of a free-list pop.
#            BumbleBee x4_seal_pool_new: +12.7% peak (pool 253.5 MB; here 1000x larger, 44.3% free).
#            Fallback: size threshold (contained SEAL patch).
# role       enabling step: while the pool retains everything, object releases cannot move the peak.
#            Free-after-paid ordering follows (CH4_MATERIAL.md 4.1; rule 6 amendment).
